# Commit messages

This file is the style. Do not run `git log` to rediscover it.

Subject is an imperative sentence that states the outcome, ending with a
period. No `feat:` / `fix:` prefix, no "Updated X", no file list. A second
paragraph is optional and is one sentence of mechanism, used when the
subject is not enough.

```
Give PLAY enough height that the knight and label sit inside the button frame.

The other root-menu rows take 0.8 of a unit so PLAY is 2.4; the board row is Centaur so that shorter cell still fits.
```

```
Keep the selected PLAY knight black, with white face, neck, and a 1px halo.
```

```
Ignore a leftover human name when a slot is Engine or Hand+Brain.
```

Bad: `Fix PLAY button layout`, `Updated menu.json and tests`, `feat: add halo`.

Changelog entries still follow `changelog.mdc`. Unobservable commits still
need a `Changelog: none -- …` trailer in the last paragraph.
